<title>SINGAPORE: India sells late Dec Cochin naphtha to Glencore.</title>
<headline>India sells late Dec Cochin naphtha to Glencore.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold by tender 30,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha to Swiss trader Glencore at $16.65 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cargo is free-on-board Cochin, on the west coast, for lifting December 22-24, they said.</p>
<p>The tender closed December 12 and was valid until December 13.</p>
<p>In its last high aromatic naphtha tender, IOC sold 25,000 tonnes to trader Vitol at $20.10 discount to Japan spot quotes for loading December 5-7 Bombay.  </p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
